  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Five-minute next-day clothing noun, agreement, pronoun, and shopping retrieval">
    <h2>Next-day retrieval</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved clothes agreement, pair agreement, and plural object reference.">
      <h3>Choose the missing form before rereading</h3>
      <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Next-day clothes and shopping choices">
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="it">it</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="them">them</button>
      </div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The rack holds a mixed group of garments: These clothes <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-hint="Clothes is plural, even though it is not a countable noun." data-fix="These clothes are ready for the display." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> ready for the display.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The label belongs to one pair: This pair of jeans <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-hint="The singular head noun pair controls the verb." data-fix="This pair of jeans is on sale." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on sale.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The customer refers back to shoes: Can I try <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="them" data-hint="Shoes is plural, so use the object pronoun them." data-fix="Can I try them on?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on?</span></div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
